{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1775","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1775","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1775\",\"parent_revision\":\"d869d12530d3a558ca2015c4a3bc2d7bb72e4b9b5f9b0704298436a786b9d0b7\",\"root_revision\":\"d869d12530d3a558ca2015c4a3bc2d7bb72e4b9b5f9b0704298436a786b9d0b7\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAppendTaskConfig (sam_schema/core/action_models.py:240) accepts task_yaml: str \u2014 a raw YAML string that is parsed and validated inside _sam_plan_append_task rather than at the MCP tool boundary. This means schema violations in the task payload are caught later in the call stack, not at the tool input layer where FastMCP/Pydantic can produce a clear structured error.\\n\\nThe problem: callers must serialize a TaskDefinition dict to YAML manually, then the server deserializes and validates it. This round-trip adds complexity and defers validation.\\n\\nThe desired outcome: AppendTaskConfig accepts a typed TaskDefinition (or an equivalent Pydantic model) directly, so Pydantic validates the task at the MCP boundary and callers pass a structured object instead of a raw YAML string.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- AppendTaskConfig is part of the public MCP tool interface (sam_plan action=append_task). Changing it is a breaking change for any caller that constructs task_yaml: str payloads.\\n- Must provide a migration path or backward-compat shim.\\n- The TaskDefinition TypedDict (task_backend_types.py:22) is the obvious target type, but TypedDict does not satisfy Pydantic's model validation directly \u2014 an equivalent Pydantic model may be needed.\\n- Investigate whether the current YAML string approach has any intentional benefits (e.g., supporting multi-document YAML or comments) before removing it.\\n\\nFlagged during review of commit fixing #1770 agent doc speculation bugs. The YAML-string design is a real API boundary smell worth addressing deliberately.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**2026-05-08 verification (grooming pass):** The 2026-04-13 fact-check described the state before the refactor. Current codebase state (verified 2026-05-08):\\n\\n- `AppendTaskConfig` NOW EXISTS at `action_models.py:272` with `task: TaskDefinition` \u2014 it is in `__all__` at line 41. The 2026-04-13 check that said it was absent was accurate at that time; the class was added as part of the refactor.\\n- `CreatePlanConfig.tasks_yaml: str` is GONE \u2014 replaced by `tasks: list[TaskDefinition]` at line 186.\\n- `_sam_plan_create` at `server.py:301` uses `config.tasks` directly; no `yaml_parser.load` and no `cast()`.\\n- `quality_gates.build_quality_gate_plan()` STILL returns a YAML string (docstring at line 122 says \\\"intended to be passed directly to `sam_create` as the `tasks_yaml` argument\\\") \u2014 this is the remaining work.\\n- `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` STILL shows `tasks_yaml=` in 4 MCP call examples.\\n- Agent docs STILL reference `tasks_yaml`.\\n\\nThe issue title remains inaccurate (describes `task_yaml: str` on `AppendTaskConfig`, but the actual refactor was `tasks_yaml: str` on `CreatePlanConfig`). Both classes are now typed; the item scope should be reframed as updating callers and docs.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-13)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n4/10 \u2014 Type safety improvement at an internal API boundary. No user-facing bug. All callers are inside this repo. Benefit is cleaner error messages and earlier validation. Low urgency; P2 is correct.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: #1139 (add task insertion skill) \u2014 any new `sam_plan` action accepting task definitions would face the same design choice and should be consistent.\\n- Bottleneck: Every caller of `sam_plan(action='create')` must serialize task dicts to YAML manually. `quality_gates.build_quality_gate_plan()` exists entirely to do this serialization.\\n- Breaking change: Any external MCP client passing `tasks_yaml` as a string field would break if the field is removed without a shim.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Schema violations in task payloads are reported by Pydantic at the MCP tool boundary with structured field-level errors, not as a generic `ValueError` deep inside `_sam_plan_create`.\\n- Callers (`swarm-task-planner`, `build_quality_gate_plan`, agent docs) pass structured dicts instead of constructing YAML strings manually.\\n- `cast(\\\"list[TaskDefinition]\\\", ...)` at `server.py:284` is eliminated \u2014 the type is guaranteed by Pydantic.\\n- `build_quality_gate_plan()` in `quality_gates.py` can return a list of task dicts instead of a YAML string, removing a serialization/deserialization round-trip.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `sam_plan(action='create')` receives a task definition with a missing required field (e.g., no `id`), the MCP tool returns a Pydantic validation error identifying the exact field and value, not a runtime exception raised during YAML parsing inside `_sam_plan_create`. Callers pass a structured list of task objects directly; no YAML serialization is required on the caller side.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- `CreatePlanConfig` has a `tasks: list[TaskDefinitionModel]` field (typed Pydantic BaseModel) instead of `tasks_yaml: str`.\\n- A `TaskDefinitionModel(BaseModel)` class exists in `action_models.py` or a shared schema module, mirroring the fields of the `TaskDefinition` TypedDict from `task_backend_types.py`.\\n- `_sam_plan_create` receives a `list[TaskDefinitionModel]` directly; no YAML parsing step inside the function.\\n- `quality_gates.build_quality_gate_plan()` returns a list of task definition dicts (or `TaskDefinitionModel` instances), not a YAML string. Its callers pass the list directly to `sam_plan`.\\n- The MCP wire format (JSON) for `sam_plan(action='create')` accepts a `tasks` array of objects, not a `tasks_yaml` string field.\\n- Existing tests in `tests_sam/` and `tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` pass without modification to their assertion logic (only the input format changes).\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `grep -n 'tasks_yaml' plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/action_models.py` returns no matches.\\n2. `grep -n 'class AppendTaskConfig\\\\|class TaskDefinitionModel' plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/action_models.py` returns a `TaskDefinitionModel` class definition (or equivalent Pydantic model in the same module or imported from a shared schema module).\\n3. `grep -rn 'cast.*TaskDefinition' plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` returns no matches.\\n4. `grep -rn 'yaml_parser.load(config.tasks' plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` returns no matches \u2014 YAML parsing of `tasks_yaml` is removed from `_sam_plan_create`.\\n5. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/ plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py -x -q` exits 0.\\n6. A test exists that passes a task definition missing the `id` field and asserts the response contains a Pydantic validation error (not a `ValueError` from YAML parsing).\\n7. `quality_gates.build_quality_gate_plan()` no longer returns a YAML string \u2014 it returns a list of task definition dicts or structured objects passable directly to the `tasks` field.\\n8. `uv run python -c 'from sam_schema.core.action_models import CreatePlanConfig; c = CreatePlanConfig(slug=\\\"s\\\", goal=\\\"g\\\", tasks=[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T1\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"t\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"not-started\\\"}]); print(c.model_dump())'` exits 0 and prints a dict with a `tasks` list.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/action_models.py` \u2014 `CreatePlanConfig` at line 144 |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_backend_types.py` \u2014 `TaskDefinition` TypedDict at line 22 (reference for field list) |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 `_sam_plan_create` at line 271; YAML parse at line 281; unsafe `cast()` at line 284 |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` \u2014 `build_quality_gate_plan()` at line 116; returns YAML string for `tasks_yaml` |\\n| Test file | `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_server.py` \u2014 `CreatePlanConfig` integration tests |\\n| Test file | `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_server_mcp.py` \u2014 MCP protocol tests using `tasks_yaml` string |\\n| Test file | `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` \u2014 taskbackend-layer tests |\\n| Agent doc | `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md:270` \u2014 MCP call example with `tasks_yaml` |\\n| Agent doc | `plugins/development-harness/agents/codebase-analyzer.md:643` \u2014 MCP call example with `tasks_yaml` |\\n| Agent doc | `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md:268` \u2014 MCP call example with `tasks_yaml` |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None (self-contained refactor).\\n- Blocks: #1139 (add task insertion skill \u2014 any new `sam_plan` action accepting task definitions should use the typed field, not another `task_yaml: str`).\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 The Pydantic model is straightforward (mirror `TaskDefinition` TypedDict fields). The blast radius is wide: `CreatePlanConfig`, `_sam_plan_create`, `build_quality_gate_plan`, 4 agent doc files, and all tests that construct `tasks_yaml` strings. Tests require mechanical update (replace YAML string with list-of-dicts). A backward-compat shim (accept both `tasks_yaml` and `tasks` during a transition window) adds complexity if external callers must be supported.\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS (partial implementation confirmed)**\\n\\nVerified against codebase 2026-05-08:\\n\\nDONE:\\n- `CreatePlanConfig` now has `tasks: list[TaskDefinition]` at `action_models.py:186` \u2014 `tasks_yaml: str` is removed.\\n- `AppendTaskConfig` now exists at `action_models.py:272` with `task: TaskDefinition` (typed Pydantic-validated field). It is exported in `__all__` at line 41.\\n- `_sam_plan_create` at `server.py:301` uses `config.tasks` directly \u2014 no `yaml_parser.load` call, no `cast()`.\\n\\nREMAINING SCOPE:\\n- `quality_gates.build_quality_gate_plan()` still returns a YAML string (docstring at line 122 still says \\\"intended to be passed directly to `sam_create` as the `tasks_yaml` argument\\\").\\n- `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` still shows `tasks_yaml=` in 4 MCP call examples (lines 144, 158, 409, 422).\\n- Agent docs (`swarm-task-planner.md`, `codebase-analyzer.md`, `feature-researcher.md`) still show `tasks_yaml` in MCP call examples.\\n\\nRT-ICA CONDITIONS:\\n- Functional intent: AVAILABLE \u2014 remaining scope is update callers to pass typed `tasks=` list instead of `tasks_yaml=` YAML string.\\n- Scope boundaries: AVAILABLE \u2014 `quality_gates.py`, `complete-implementation/SKILL.md`, 3 agent docs.\\n- External interfaces: AVAILABLE \u2014 MCP boundary already accepts typed `tasks` list; no additional interface changes needed.\\n- Constraints: AVAILABLE \u2014 must not break tests; existing tests referencing `tasks_yaml` need mechanical update.\\n- Existing system context: AVAILABLE \u2014 all affected files identified and listed in Resources.\\n- Verification expectations: AVAILABLE \u2014 acceptance criteria (1), (3), (4) are already satisfied; (7) and agent doc criteria remain open.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **replace appendtaskconfig.task_yaml: str with typed taskdefinition parameter** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Code review during #1770 fix \u2014 user-flagged design smell when fixing speculation bugs in agent docs\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-13\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"665014eed42bc19033d9dab393a8bd7432e1d12aec14c307633dbca93fec463c\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS-cmA\"}"}